    <p class="title is-5 mathjax">
      
        GLU Attention Improve Transformer
      
    </p>
    <p class="authors">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Authors:</span>
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Wang%2C+Z">Zehao Wang</a>
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2507.00022v2-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        &hellip;a novel attention mechanism called GLU Attention, which introduces nonlinearity into the values of Attention. My experiments demonstrate that GLU Attention improves both <span class="search-hit mathjax">model</span> performance and convergence speed across text and vision modalities with zero additional parameters and negligible computational costs. GLU Attention is lightweight and can seamlessly&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2507.00022v2-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2507.00022v2-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2507.00022v2-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        Gated Linear Units (GLU) have shown great potential in enhancing neural network performance. In this paper, I introduce a novel attention mechanism called GLU Attention, which introduces nonlinearity into the values of Attention. My experiments demonstrate that GLU Attention improves both <span class="search-hit mathjax">model</span> performance and convergence speed across text and vision modalities with zero additional parameters and negligible computational costs. GLU Attention is lightweight and can seamlessly integrate with other technologies, such as Flash Attention, Rotary Position Embedding (RoPE), and various Multi-Head Attention (MHA) variants such as Grouped-Query Attention (GQA). This project is open-sourced at github.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2507.00022v2-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2507.00022v2-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

